O let that Mercy of Thine, which has spared us so long, at last lead us to Repentance, that we may forsake our evil Ways, and turn unto Thee the Lord our God before that dreadful Day comes upon us, when all Opportunity of reconciling our selves to our offended God, shall be far from us. Give us Grace, O Lord, seriously to consider the great Work we have to do, and the Uncertainty of that Time which Thou hast given us to perform it in, that we may not be so foolish as to consume our Days in Vanity and Folly, in satisfying our corrupt Inclinations, indulging our vicious Appetites; but grant that we may walk before Thee in such a holy and religious Manner, with that Fear of Thy Divine Majesty, that Dread of Thy Displeasure, and with such an earnest Solicitude after the Things of another Life, that we may daily grow in Grace, and he continually advancing towards an happy Eternity.

